From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:35:00 +0100
Subject: mediatek: apsoc: halt on system off instead of reset

Filogic boards have no power-off control. PSCI SYSTEM_OFF did a
watchdog reset, so a shutdown rebooted the board. Stop the watchdog
and halt the CPU instead.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
--- a/plat/mediatek/apsoc_common/bl31/plat_pm.c
+++ b/plat/mediatek/apsoc_common/bl31/plat_pm.c
@@ -363,10 +363,13 @@
 static void __dead2 mtk_plat_system_off(void)
 {
 	console_switch_state(CONSOLE_FLAG_BOOT);
-	ERROR("Power-down unsupported.\n");
-	console_switch_state(CONSOLE_FLAG_RUNTIME);
+	NOTICE("MTK System Off: no power-off control, halting\n");
+	mtk_wdt_control(false);
+	console_flush();
 
-	mtk_plat_system_reset();
+	/* the boards have no PMIC power-off line, so halt instead of reset */
+	while (1)
+		wfi();
 }
 
 #pragma weak mtk_plat_system_reset2
